---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const noSlash = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const u = (p: string) => `${noSlash}${p}`;
---

<ContentLayout
  title="How we work: weeks, not months | Freedom45"
  description="How Freedom45 works with startups and public bodies: a working prototype in weeks, then build, grow and long-term support. You talk to the people building it."
  activePage="how-we-work"
>
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
    <h1>Weeks, <span class="g">not months.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">Most software doesn't fail because of the code. It fails because nobody found out early enough what its users actually needed. We put something real in front of people fast, then build on what works.</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-n step-n--explore" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div>
          <h3><span class="stage stage--explore">Explore:</span> test it before you commit</h3>
          <p>We prototype with AI-first tools to test the riskiest part of the idea first, in weeks.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>We start with a working session on the problem, the people it's for and the riskiest assumption.</li>
            <li>We build a working prototype and put it in front of real users.</li>
            <li>You get a clear plan for the build: what's in it, how long it should take and what it should cost.</li>
            <li>You decide whether to build it, change it, or stop with your budget intact.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-n step-n--build" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div>
          <h3><span class="stage stage--build">Build:</span> ship the product</h3>
          <p>We turn what you've proven into a product or service people can rely on, accessible from day one.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>We build in short cycles, with something new you can open and try each time, not a status report.</li>
            <li>Accessibility and security are built in as we go, not bolted on at the end.</li>
            <li>At launch you get the product, the hosting set up (ours or your own) and documentation so anyone can pick it up.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-n step-n--grow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div>
          <h3><span class="stage stage--grow">Grow:</span> take it to the next stage</h3>
          <p>Performance, the next features, and the code health a growing product needs.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Features and performance work, guided by how people actually use it, so it holds up before it starts to creak.</li>
            <li>Solid processes around the code: automated testing, safe releases and a clear way to handle problems when they happen.</li>
            <li>Ready for funding: architecture and security documentation, running costs you can explain, and support through investors' technical due diligence. Our founders have lived this already: three funding rounds and an acquisition.</li>
            <li>We work with you on the long-term roadmap and technical strategy, so what we build next matches where the business is going.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-n step-n--sustain" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div>
          <h3><span class="stage stage--sustain">Sustain:</span> keep it running</h3>
          <p>Support, fixes and upkeep long after go-live, and we'll happily look after something we didn't build.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Monitoring and alerts, so we spot problems before your users do.</li>
            <li>Security and dependency updates kept current, with regular health checks of the code and the hosting.</li>
            <li>Support for you and your users: when something goes wrong, you get the people who built it.</li>
            <li>Running costs reviewed so you're not paying for what you don't use, and documentation kept up to date so the product never depends on one person.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What it's like to work with us</h2>
    <div class="cards cards--2">
      <div class="card"><h3>You talk to the builders</h3><p>No account managers in between. The people you speak to are the people building it.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>You see it working</h3><p>Something you can open and try, early and often.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we use AI</h2>
    <p>We use AI a lot, because it gets you results faster: prototypes in weeks, and more of your budget spent on the parts that matter. A person oversees it and checks everything before it reaches you, and we're open about where and how we use it.</p>
  </section>

</ContentLayout>
